content:
An editor is not just a component — it is a component paired with metadata saying which document type it handles. That pairing is an `EditorModule`, typed in `packages/shared/document-model/types.ts`:

```ts
export type EditorModule<TProps = any> = {
  Component: FC<EditorProps & TProps>;
  documentTypes: string[];
  config: { id: string; name: string };
};
```

`documentTypes` is an array, so one module can serve several document types. `EditorProps` is deliberately minimal — `{ children?, className?, document? }` — because the modern pattern is for the component to reach the document through a generated hook rather than through props.

Codegen emits the module next to the component and wraps the import in `lazy()` so the editor is code-split:

```ts
// editors/todo-editor/module.ts
export const TodoEditor: EditorModule = {
  Component: lazy(() => import("./editor.js")),
  documentTypes: ["powerhouse/todo"],
  config: { id: "todo-editor", name: "Todo Editor" },
};
```

The registry itself is `editors/editors.ts`, a barrel collecting every module into one array. The boilerplate template ships it with an empty array and a `WARNING: DO NOT EDIT / auto-generated and updated by codegen` header:

```ts
import type { EditorModule } from "document-model";
import { TodoEditor } from "./todo-editor/module.js";

export const editors: EditorModule[] = [TodoEditor];
```

When a user opens a document, the host looks up which editor is registered for that document type and mounts it. If nothing is registered, there is no UI — no error, no fallback. The academy is blunt about the consequence: a missing registration is **the most common reason an editor doesn't appear in Connect**. Because the file is codegen-owned, the failure mode is usually a codegen run that did not update the barrel, not hand-written code — so when a freshly scaffolded editor does not show up, check the array before debugging the component.

_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/04-editors/{01-what-is-an-editor,02-your-first-editor}.mdx, confirmed against packages/shared/document-model/types.ts and packages/codegen/src/templates/boilerplate/editors/editors.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._
